s5-release.summaryMarkdown:
REL-1 holds. `ServiceResolutionError` (`crates/rayx_core/src/di/registry.rs`) and `AppError` (`crates/rayx_app/src/surface.rs`) are `#[non_exhaustive]`, and nothing else in the source changed (d-error-enums: only the two enums, no sealed commit rewritten). Each enum has a passing doc test with a wildcard arm. Each also has a `compile_fail` test that names exactly the enum's current variants (all nine of `AppError`, all four of `ServiceResolutionError`), so non-exhaustiveness is the only thing that can make it fail. The check logs show 2 doc tests per enum, the compile-fail one included. Nothing outside the two defining crates matches either enum. `aa2217c`'s `Migration: apps:` footers match the code:
- the wildcard arm;
- `MissingKey`, `WrongThread` and `Failed` with their fields;
- `AppError::NoApp` gone and `BuilderStarted` new;
- `start_app` gone in favour of `start` / `start_async`;
- the full old-to-new mapping into `rayx_app::ts`, matching the pre-epic root and prelude exports (`I18n`, `Navigation`, `NavigationRegion`, `Storage`, `Platform`, `AppConfiguration`, `Assets`, `Fonts` and the i18n value types);
- the attribute form, overriding the earlier `native_module!` note.
The commit has no AI attribution and touches no forbidden path. The FR-2 memory repair (the app/tsx decision record) is correct but still uncommitted; it should go into the s5 seal commit.
